{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LrCS88Q25MnWXE2huCpuR3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: pi-lhc-epic-01-connector-core-build\n3\tdescription: Autonomous orchestration (impl-lead) of the pi-lhc Epic 1 Connector Core build via lbuild-impl ls-impl; durable run state lives in team-impl-log.md.\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: c60a53bf-54ba-4447-8e83-5ae7d2b4edb8\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tLee tasked an autonomous, long-horizon orchestration (I am impl-lead) of the **pi-lhc Epic 1 \"Connector Core\"** build using the `lbuild-impl` CLI + `ls-impl` skill. Spec pack root: `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/` (epic.md, tech-design.md, test-plan.md, stories 00-foundation … 06-startup-validation). pi-lhc is a PI extension that hosts the LHC SDK (`packages/pi-lhc`, workspace-depends on `packages/lhc`). Epic 1 is **observe-only**: capture PI hook traffic into LHC threads, derive LHC turns from PI traffic (PI fires turn-per-step; one LHC turn = whole exchange, closed at agent_end), route derivation inference through PI's auth — change nothing the model sees.\n11\t\n12\t**Why:** Multi-story provider-backed build spanning hours; state must survive context compaction and session restarts, so it is kept on disk, not in conversation.\n13\t\n14\t**How to apply:** On resume, read `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md` FIRST (it holds State, Current Story, Current Phase, story receipts, baselines, continuation handles) plus `impl-run.config.json` and `artifacts/`, and continue from the recorded State — do NOT reconstruct from memory of prior turns. Provider config: story-lead+verifier+quick-fixer = codex/gpt-5.5, implementor = claude-opus-4-8/max (codex auth confirmed working). Story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`; epic gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all`. Stories touching `packages/lhc` (e.g. Story 1's A-8 registry additions) also need `pnpm --filter lhc verify` at acceptance since configured gates are pi-lhc-scoped. Commit per accepted story on `main` with scoped pathspecs — a large pre-existing lhc-docs reorg (~1267 entries) sits staged in the index; keep it OUT of story commits. Long provider runs: background them and watch with a ~5-min Monitor on the status.json until terminal. See [[lbuild-impl-needs-ruling-on-implementor-deviations]].\n15\t\n16\t**Recurring failure modes + recovery (observed across Stories 1-2):** (1) SILENCE STALL — a story-continue resuming a large claude-code session goes silent and hits the silence timeout; fixed by raising `story_implementor_silence_timeout_ms` to 1200000 (20m) in impl-run.config.json (done). (2) LARGE-OUTPUT PARSE FAILURE — claude-code provider operations (implement OR continue) that emit more than ~1MB of streaming stdout fail at finalize with `PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID` (\"stdout was not exact JSON\"; the runtime stops the process as 'stale' and can't parse the result envelope). This blocks from-scratch implements/continues on LARGE stories. CRITICAL: claude-code APPLIES EDITS LIVE as it streams, so even when the result envelope fails to parse, the code changes ARE on disk. RECOVERY for the large-output case: do NOT keep retrying ever-larger implement/continue ops. Instead (a) gate the on-disk state (`pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`) to confirm it's coherent, then (b) run a FRESH primitive `story-verify` (verifier output is bounded, so it finalizes fine) to get an authoritative verdict on the on-disk code, then (c) accept if it passes, or use `quick-fix` (small bounded output) for focused remaining findings + re-verify. Drive acceptance with impl-lead authority (receipt + commit) outside the stuck composed loop when needed. (3) Transient codex story-lead PLANNER output-invalid on a turn — a plain `story-orchestrate resume` retries the planner turn. (4) Broken/unstable session resume — reopen review-request directing a fresh run-implement. (5) CODEX RESUME DRIFT — a codex story-verify FOLLOW-UP (resume) fails PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID \"Codex resume schema drift\" (resume can't take --output-schema); for re-verification always use a FRESH story-verify (initial mode) with post-fix context, never a follow-up. (6) For fixes when claude-code can't finalize (>1MB), the CODEX quick_fixer + a fresh codex story-verify is the reliable loop (codex doesn't share claude's size bug). When a verifier keeps surfacing ever-narrower edges of the SAME finding, stop piecemeal-patching: reason about whether the failing input is reachable in PRODUCTION (check the real PI hook contract in notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md) — real PI message_end ALWAYS carries a stable entry id (research line ~142 \"every entry carries id+parentId\"), so id-less/position-less collision repros are synthetic/unreachable and can be accepted-risk with a hardening note rather than chased forever.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d6d1f63-412d-4ec0-a1d3-5b6b004b453c","uuid":"f38c554f-8afa-420e-80ef-23b8c32a1c6d","timestamp":"2026-06-14T10:44:56.150Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/.claude/projects/-Users-leemoore-code-pi-long-horizon-liminal-context/memory/pi-lhc-epic-01-connector-core-build.md","content":"---\nname: pi-lhc-epic-01-connector-core-build\ndescription: Autonomous orchestration (impl-lead) of the pi-lhc Epic 1 Connector Core build via lbuild-impl ls-impl; durable run state lives in team-impl-log.md.\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c60a53bf-54ba-4447-8e83-5ae7d2b4edb8\n---\n\nLee tasked an autonomous, long-horizon orchestration (I am impl-lead) of the **pi-lhc Epic 1 \"Connector Core\"** build using the `lbuild-impl` CLI + `ls-impl` skill. Spec pack root: `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/` (epic.md, tech-design.md, test-plan.md, stories 00-foundation … 06-startup-validation). pi-lhc is a PI extension that hosts the LHC SDK (`packages/pi-lhc`, workspace-depends on `packages/lhc`). Epic 1 is **observe-only**: capture PI hook traffic into LHC threads, derive LHC turns from PI traffic (PI fires turn-per-step; one LHC turn = whole exchange, closed at agent_end), route derivation inference through PI's auth — change nothing the model sees.\n\n**Why:** Multi-story provider-backed build spanning hours; state must survive context compaction and session restarts, so it is kept on disk, not in conversation.\n\n**How to apply:** On resume, read `docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md` FIRST (it holds State, Current Story, Current Phase, story receipts, baselines, continuation handles) plus `impl-run.config.json` and `artifacts/`, and continue from the recorded State — do NOT reconstruct from memory of prior turns. Provider config: story-lead+verifier+quick-fixer = codex/gpt-5.5, implementor = claude-opus-4-8/max (codex auth confirmed working). Story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`; epic gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all`. Stories touching `packages/lhc` (e.g. Story 1's A-8 registry additions) also need `pnpm --filter lhc verify` at acceptance since configured gates are pi-lhc-scoped. Commit per accepted story on `main` with scoped pathspecs — a large pre-existing lhc-docs reorg (~1267 entries) sits staged in the index; keep it OUT of story commits. Long provider runs: background them and watch with a ~5-min Monitor on the status.json until terminal. See [[lbuild-impl-needs-ruling-on-implementor-deviations]].\n\n**Recurring failure modes + recovery (observed across Stories 1-2):** (1) SILENCE STALL — a story-continue resuming a large claude-code session goes silent and hits the silence timeout; fixed by raising `story_implementor_silence_timeout_ms` to 1200000 (20m) in impl-run.config.json (done). (2) LARGE-OUTPUT PARSE FAILURE — claude-code provider operations (implement OR continue) that emit more than ~1MB of streaming stdout fail at finalize with `PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID` (\"stdout was not exact JSON\"; the runtime stops the process as 'stale' and can't parse the result envelope). This blocks from-scratch implements/continues on LARGE stories. CRITICAL: claude-code APPLIES EDITS LIVE as it streams, so even when the result envelope fails to parse, the code changes ARE on disk. RECOVERY for the large-output case: do NOT keep retrying ever-larger implement/continue ops. Instead (a) gate the on-disk state (`pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`) to confirm it's coherent, then (b) run a FRESH primitive `story-verify` (verifier output is bounded, so it finalizes fine) to get an authoritative verdict on the on-disk code, then (c) accept if it passes, or use `quick-fix` (small bounded output) for focused remaining findings + re-verify. Drive acceptance with impl-lead authority (receipt + commit) outside the stuck composed loop when needed. (3) Transient codex story-lead PLANNER output-invalid on a turn — a plain `story-orchestrate resume` retries the planner turn. (4) Broken/unstable session resume — reopen review-request directing a fresh run-implement. (5) CODEX RESUME DRIFT — a codex story-verify FOLLOW-UP (resume) fails PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID \"Codex resume schema drift\" (resume can't take --output-schema); for re-verification always use a FRESH story-verify (initial mode) with post-fix context, never a follow-up. (6) For fixes when claude-code can't finalize (>1MB), the CODEX quick_fixer + a fresh codex story-verify is the reliable loop (codex doesn't share claude's size bug). When a verifier keeps surfacing ever-narrower edges of the SAME finding, stop piecemeal-patching: reason about whether the failing input is reachable in PRODUCTION (check the real PI hook contract in notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md) — real PI message_end ALWAYS carries a stable entry id (research line ~142 \"every entry carries id+parentId\"), so id-less/position-less collision repros are synthetic/unreachable and can be accepted-risk with a hardening note rather than chased forever.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}}}
